It is also possible to do a total (vs differential) flash using qfirehose. Due to limited free space on the NR7101 you will have to use a client/server scheme (client is linux PC, server is NR7101). 
Qfirehose for linux can be found at [[https://github.com/Biktorgj/qfirehose]]. Download zip and unpack to a convenient folder.
You can get the firmware from ROOter [[https://www.ofmodemsandmen.com/mfirm.html]]. Download zip and unpack to a convenient folder.

  * NR7101 as server:
<code>
root@RT2NR7101:~# qfirehose -p 9008
</code>
  * Linux PC as client (firmware was unpacked in subfolder RG502Q):
<code>
bruker@linux:~$ bin/QFirehose -f RG502Q/ -p <nr7101-ip>:9008
...
